   "title": "The two readers disagreed on style in 57 scripts",
   "happened": "Every accepted script was read by two agents, each alone, against a seven-item checklist; no person read them. The Claude reader passed all 307. The GPT-6.2 reader passed 250 and flagged 57 on two style items only: top-level code in the script (55) and two extra standard HOL4 theories (2). Neither reader found a soundness problem.",
   "done": "Ruled at 16:19 UTC, before the key was opened: a flag on one of those two style items alone, with the other reader passing and no flag on the five other items, does not exclude an attempt. All 57 are listed, with both readers’ reasons, in the scoring report.",
