   "title": "Two findings",
   "text": "A Claude agent reports that the judge’s log can be read across families, and that a planted statement can hold vacuously."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T13:42:00Z",
   "title": "The log is put off limits",
   "text": "The 4 running Claude agents are told not to read it."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T13:47:00Z",
   "title": "Two rulings",
   "text": "Agents read the accepted scripts; the gate judges what the kernel judged."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T13:51:00Z",
   "title": "Material from before the run moved out",
   "text": "A Claude agent’s report shows it could be read; it is moved out of the agents’ reach."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T13:54:03Z",
   "title": "The GPT-6.2 Astra family finishes",
   "text": "All 9 of its batches have ended."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T15:09:00Z",
   "title": "The Claude Opus 5.5 family finishes",
   "text": "All 9 of its batches have ended."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T15:09:00Z",
   "title": "The run ends",
   "text": "Every statement is judged or at the cap for both families, or the run was stopped."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T15:29:00Z",
   "title": "The first blinding audit",
   "text": "A Claude agent reads every agent’s tool log: the GPT family is clean, six of the nine Claude agents are not."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T16:04:00Z",
   "title": "Every accepted proof rebuilt",
   "text": "307 of 307 rebuilt alone, with the same decision; the judge machine is deleted."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T16:08:00Z",
   "title": "The second blinding audit",
   "text": "A GPT-6.2 agent audits the same logs on its own and agrees on every read that matters."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T16:19:00Z",
   "title": "Both readers done, and a ruling",
   "text": "No reader finds a soundness problem; style-only flags do not exclude an attempt."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T16:45:00Z",
   "title": "The key is unlocked, and the run scored",
   "text": "The gate holds in both families."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T17:10:00Z",
   "title": "The slab soundness theorem",
   "text": "The one true statement neither family proved is finished by a builder that had read the key, and the slab theorem is assembled."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-25T17:53:00Z",
   "title": "Layer 1 holds",
   "text": "The three soundness theorems, and the five certificates through them."
