 "next": [
  {
   "title": "The CakeML job on CI",
   "short": "CakeML on CI",
   "state": "started 19:37 UTC, running",
   "text": "The repository’s replay runs on every push. Its second job, which also builds CakeML’s basis, translates and compiles the checker and runs the binary on all 52 inputs, runs by hand or weekly. It was started by hand at 19:37 UTC and is expected to take about 3 h; until it ends, it has not run on a standard CI runner nor in the repository’s own layout."
  },
  {
   "title": "A bridge to Lean, as a plan",
   "short": "Lean bridge",
   "state": "a plan; one trial so far",
   "text": "The plan: decide the certificates in Lean’s own kernel as well, read the data back and refuse the forgeries there, and set the result beside the Lean formalisation of the full statement by Snively. So far one slab has been decided in Lean’s kernel, as a trial before the run, in 807 s (HOL4: 1.15 s); the other four have no Lean verdict."
  },
  {
   "title": "The dominance lemma, offered to HOL4",
   "short": "HOL4 pull request",
   "state": "prepared, not opened",
   "text": "The lemma that weighted diagonal dominance gives positive (semi)definiteness is prepared as a pull request to the HOL4 repository. Opening it is Carlos Toledo’s step; nothing has been sent."
  }
 ],
